// PD-dedicated Brandon Amaro 2022 orchestral score, read from vector noteheads, clefs, accidentals, stems, beams, dots and printed tuplets; reduced original instrumentation: flute 1, oboes, bassoon 1, violin I, viola and cello. All 88 bars, including the opening E-horn F# octave, bassoon accompaniment, pizzicato cello theme and later high woodwind/string answers. Printed quintuplets and measured string tremolo keep their written beat positions. Same accepted tempo, meter and end; ties are sustained, pizzicato/arco uses fixed GM parts, no custom banks. Other wind/brass/percussion and second string parts omitted; grace ornaments omitted without shifting main notes. Dynamics use explicit levels, hairpins and fine articulations are not fully realized.
